docs/glossary.md:10:One investigation: a Goal and the DesignQuestions, Hypotheses, Experiments and Results under it, kept as events in one store. The binary is `hyp`; "tree" stays the concept name ([spec §1](replay-spec.md#1-names-and-locations)).
docs/glossary.md:42:A Goal whose candidate is a claim: what to build, or why something behaves as it does. Rival Hypotheses answer each DesignQuestion, and Experiments separate them, often from a pinned recipe whose rubric turns its measures into verdicts. A line names a case every candidate must meet that a check can run on every candidate. A discovery Goal whose questions the owner settles by argument in a session, with the session as evidence, is a design record: no run checks its candidates, so it has no lines, and its cases go to the lines of the build Goal that follows it.
docs/glossary.md:104:How an Experiment's measures become verdicts, fixed before the run. It is the kind of Bundle kept in `rubrics/`, apart from recipes, so two Experiments can pin the same one; it has no step section and its one command reads the measures in the Experiment's records and prints a `verdict: LABEL=WORD` line per label, with a supports case and a contradicts case for each label among its known answers; or, when the verdicts are decided by reading, prose in the Experiment's body, which only its author and a reader of the Result can hold to one reading. A rubric names no tree id: the runner gives each label's verdict to its target in `hyp record`. An Experiment with no targets has no rubric.
docs/glossary.md:115:One `evidence` entry of a Result: a URL, a path under `.tree/evidence/`, or `recipes/NAME@N/FILE`, which hyp looks up like a recipe ref and pins by its bundle hash ([spec §4](replay-spec.md#4-event-types-closed-set), [spec §7.6](replay-spec.md#76-experiments-and-results)). `event.EvidenceRef` reads the ref of the last kind.
docs/glossary.md:119:A recipe ref and the bundle hash an event recorded for it when it was written: an Experiment's recipe, or an evidence pointer into a versioned bundle ([spec §7.6](replay-spec.md#76-experiments-and-results)). In code: `replay.Pin`, listed per Result in `replay.Res.Pins`.
docs/glossary.md:123:A Result one of whose pins no longer matches the current recipe hashes, because its bundle changed or is missing ([spec §7.6](replay-spec.md#76-experiments-and-results), `questionable_evidence`). It is a flag only and never changes a status. In code: `replay.Res.Questionable`.
docs/glossary.md:219:An edge that replaces its target. Between two Hypotheses under one question, a rival claim replaces the old one, which reads superseded ([spec §7.1](replay-spec.md#71-hypothesis-status-first-matching-rule-wins)). Between two Experiments, a new procedure replaces one with no live Result, which is then closed ([spec §7.6](replay-spec.md#76-experiments-and-results), ADR 0008).
docs/glossary.md:285:The set of recipe versions a repository keeps, which Experiments cite instead of copying.
